{"availability":"available","full":"3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock","name":"34-ApocalyptiClock","description":"A live, AI-generated reading of existential risk, updated every 4 hours from real news headlines. Not affiliated with the official Doomsday Clock.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-07T18:40:28Z","updated":"2026-10-10T04:12:05Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://3rebus4byss.github.io/34-ApocalyptiClock/","topics":["ai","apocalypse-clock","doomsday-clock","end-of-days-clock","gdelt","github-actions","github-pages","news","risk-assessment"],"demo":"https://3rebus4byss.github.io/34-ApocalyptiClock/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.882Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.882Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.882Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.882Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every 4 hours, this checks real headlines for one risk category at a time — nuclear, conflict, climate, biosecurity, AI risk, or information warfare (misinformation, disinformation, propaganda) — rotating through all six over a 24-hour span. Since there are 6 categories and 6 runs/day (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 UTC), each category lands on the exact same clock time every day. An AI model (Gemini, free tier) gives a grounded, cited judgment: did that category's risk move up, down, or hold, and why, citing the specific stories behind the call — with awareness of the category's…","Runs entirely on GitHub's servers via GitHub Actions — not your local machine. It keeps running whether your computer is on, off, or unplugged. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, free, no credit card, no credit-based billing to run out of.","No random numbers, no canned phrases. If a category's news fetch or the model's judgment fails for its turn, that category is simply left unchanged until its next scheduled check rather than faked."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"adcc4f0cc6370f4675df0b7fa77fdd48dbc3bc355b75cba86714bcdfe8a9115e","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.981Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.981Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Every 4 hours, this checks real headlines for one risk category at a time — nuclear, conflict, climate, biosecurity, AI risk, or information warfare (misinformation, disinformation, propaganda) — rotating through all six over a 24-hour span. Since there are 6 categories and 6 runs/day (00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 UTC), each category lands on the exact same clock time every day. An AI model (Gemini, free tier) gives a grounded, cited judgment: did that category's risk move up, down, or hold, and why, citing the specific stories behind the call — with awareness of the category's…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Go to sign in with any Google account, click \"Create API key.\"","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Go to sign in with any Google account, click \"Create API key.\"","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Sign up at gdeltcloud.com/auth/sign-up, get a key at gdeltcloud.com/api-keys.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"adcc4f0cc6370f4675df0b7fa77fdd48dbc3bc355b75cba86714bcdfe8a9115e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3rebus4byss/34-ApocalyptiClock/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:17.981Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T04:12:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/3